      },
      "rev_n_1_3e99c3_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_3e99c3_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_3e99c3",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of simulating the torpedo's movement and checking for collisions is correct, but it's not efficient enough for large inputs. The issue is that we're storing all ship positions in a set, which can be memory-intensive for large numbers of ships. Instead, we can use a more efficient approach by checking the ship positions directly as we simulate the torpedo's movement. This will reduce both time and space complexity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_3e99c3_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9cfc2821d0",
        "created_at": 1794534813.1463428
      },
      "rev_n_2_83aef8_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_83aef8_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_83aef8",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was in the decision-making process for the torpedo's movement. The current approach always moves right when there's a ship, which is not optimal for avoiding all ships. Instead, we should consider the positions of all active ships and choose the move that minimizes the risk of hitting any ship. This requires a more sophisticated decision-making algorithm that takes into account the positions of all active ships simultaneously.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_83aef8_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_da9e10f853",
        "created_at": 1794534847.0600383
      },
      "rev_n_3_a8e5d2_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_a8e5d2_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_a8e5d2",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of always moving the torpedo towards the nearest ship is not optimal. It fails because it doesn't consider the possibility of waiting at a position to avoid multiple ships simultaneously. A better strategy would be to use a sweep line algorithm, moving the torpedo to cover all ships in a single pass, while ensuring it doesn't hit any.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_a8e5d2_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_055ad67632",
        "created_at": 1794534889.798014
      },
